WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.840
It’s crazy when you think about all of
the different kinds of foods we eat.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.760
We just swallow and hope
it all works out for the best.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.280
Well, as it turns out,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.680
there are better ways to think about keeping
our bodies humming healthfully along.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.080
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.120
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.280
In this episode, Dr. Kristine Dennis takes
a deep dive into the research

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.160
around raising plant-based kids!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.600
Dr. Dennis is our new
Senior Research Scientist

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.880
who also happens to
be a plant-based parent.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.120
We start with a story about how
eating well-balanced plant-based diets

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.720
during pregnancy can reduce
risks of gestational diabetes

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.600
and hypertensive disorders
like preeclampsia.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.360
Over the past two decades,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.960
scientific and
professional nutrition,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.480
and pediatric associations,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.680
have issued official statements
and published position papers

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.440
about adopting vegan diets
during crucial life stages,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.360
including pregnancy
and lactation,

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.040
infancy, and childhood.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.640
While some of these associations

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.280
firmly agree
a well-designed vegan diet

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.480
can be healthy and support
normal growth and development,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.320
others are more reserved,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.760
and some caution against
vegan diets for children.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.960
Those that are supportive

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.200
include the American
Dietetic Association,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.400
which has held this position
for more than 25 years,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.160
as well as
professional associations

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.280
in Australia, Canada,
Portugal, Italy,

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.840
the UK, Finland,
Germany, and Norway,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.920
and Europe more broadly.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.480
More reserved opinions
also came out of the UK

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.880
and Europe, including Spain,

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.960
and downright
dismissive positions

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.400
have come out of Slovenia,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.040
Germany, Italy,
France, and Belgium.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.320
What does the evidence say
about vegan diets in children?

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.800
Part of the challenge
starts at the very beginning,

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.480
with the exclusion
of pregnant people

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.320
from clinical trials in general.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.680
With such compelling needs,

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.520
why are pregnant women
largely excluded

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.800
from clinical research?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.040
Often due to ethical concerns,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.200
dominated by fears
of fetal harm.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.760
Even non-pregnant women
of reproductive age

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.520
often have to commit
to contraception

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.040
during the research period,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.400
and those who become pregnant

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.120
must leave the study
with their data excluded.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.480
That all adds up to a lack
of clinical trial data

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.840
on pregnant women.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.720
Paradoxically,
these precautionary measures

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.360
may not have made pregnant moms
or their babies safer

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.680
because of the resulting
lack of evidence.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.240
Some of the commentary
around vegan diets for children

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.520
includes this same concern
about the lack of data.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.880
One researcher stated,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.920
"In children we do not
have many good quality studies,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.600
and the studies we do have come
mostly from vegetarian children,

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.000
and they are of
very varying quality."

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.800
But researchers are
attempting to fill this void,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.960
starting with,
"To vegan or not to vegan

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.680
when pregnant, lactating,
or feeding young children."

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.440
The oldest
and largest association

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.360
of nutritional professionals
in the world,

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.000
the Academy
of Nutrition and Dietetics

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
considers a completely
plant-based diet

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.680
to be suitable during pregnancy,

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.000
lactation, infancy,
and childhood,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.760
provided it is well-planned.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.840
What exactly
does well-planned mean?

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.000
First of all, a diet
rich in a wide variety

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.320
of plant foods;
grains, legumes

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.120
(such as beans, lentils,
split peas, and chickpeas),

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.280
fruits and veggies,
nuts and seeds,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.480
herbs and spices.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.000
We want to limit vegetable fats

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.880
so they don't displace
more nutrient-dense foods,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.840
and if you do use them,
choosing them carefully,

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.640
for example, avoiding
trans fats and tropical oils.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.320
Also taking a DHA supplement,
consuming enough calcium,

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.480
and ensuring
sufficient vitamin D.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.840
And most importantly,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.400
not forgetting
about vitamin B12,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.040
as Dr. Greger
has covered extensively

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.760
because it is so important
to ensure a regular

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.880
and reliable source
of vitamin B12.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.240
Balanced plant-based diets

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.080
mean eating a wide
variety of plant foods

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.960
in order to sufficiently
meet energy requirements,

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.800
and paying attention
to some nutrients

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.200
that may be critical,
iodine included.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.600
It's one nutrient that
should also be supplemented

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.520
during pregnancy
and breastfeeding.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.120
What are the impacts
on the mother's health

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.680
of following a vegetarian diet
during pregnancy?

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.320
Gestational diabetes
affects around 14 percent

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.000
of pregnancies globally,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.400
and even more
in some regions of the world.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.400
It's also at the center
of the vicious cycle

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.120
of diabetes begetting diabetes.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.040
Linked not only
to adverse pregnancy

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.640
and birth outcomes,

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.120
but greater long-term risk
of cardiometabolic disorders

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.920
for both moms and babies.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.680
Research suggests
beneficial impacts

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.080
of plant-based diets
on blood sugar control.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.680
What effect might that have
on risk of gestational diabetes?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.600
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.120
on plant-based
dietary patterns

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.240
and gestational diabetes risk
found that those who ate

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.320
closer to a healthy,
plant-based diet

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.320
had a significantly lower risk

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.800
of developing
gestational diabetes.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.120
Evidence from the
Harvard Nurses' Health Study II

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.080
suggests these benefits extend
to hypertensive disorders,

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.680
like preeclampsia,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.360
with a 20 percent lower risk

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.800
among those eating
the most plant-based diets.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.040
And this lower risk
could benefit moms' health

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.480
for years to come,

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.880
as hypertensive disorders
during pregnancy

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.120
are associated with
increased risk of stroke

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.240
later in life.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.240
Note that Dr. Greger
previously covered

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.362
other pregnancy
outcomes, as well.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.600
In our next story, 
Dr. Kristine Dennis looks at the studies

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.880
on the IQs
of vegetarian children.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.480
Many vegetarian parents believe

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.520
their children are brighter
than omnivorous kids,

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.040
but you don't really know
until you put it to the test.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.600
And, indeed,
the IQ of vegetarian children

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.720
tested about 16 points
higher than average,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.440
and their mental age exceeded
their chronological age

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.120
by about a year.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.760
The researchers knew
the veg kids were bright,

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.120
but why were they
so much more superior?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.880
There are obviously
confounding factors,

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.040
like maybe more highly
educated parents

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.360
are more likely to have
vegetarian children,

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.880
and they pass down both
their brains and their diets.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.280
Even if there is
a cause-and-effect relationship

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.680
between vegetarianism and IQ,

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.800
were the children smarter
because they were vegetarians,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.240
or did they become vegetarian
because they were so smart?

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.760
Researchers in the UK followed
8,000 kids for decades.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.000
They measured their IQ
at age 10,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.520
then came back 20 years later

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:09.520
and asked which of them had
become vegetarian during that time.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.080
And, indeed, the smarter kids
had an increased likelihood

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.640
of being a vegetarian
as an adult.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.040
The researchers even quoted
Benjamin Franklin,

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.680
saying that vegetarian
diets result in

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.120
"Greater clearness of head
and quicker comprehension."

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.440
According to the largest
and oldest association

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.840
of nutrition professionals
in the world,

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.760
strictly plant-based
diets are appropriate

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.000
for all stages of
the life cycle,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.440
including childhood,

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.240
and may indeed
provide health benefits.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.360
What about plant-based diets
and growth in children?

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.800
Some studies show that children

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.200
raised on restrictive
macrobiotic diets

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.040
suffer from growth stunting,

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.600
while others show
that those raised plant-based

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.560
may end up being
up to an inch (2.5 cm) taller.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.480
In a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.680
of children on vegan diets,
heights were lower in vegans,

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.840
but only because
they included a study

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.280
in which the vegan kids
were significantly younger,

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.680
mostly 10 to 14 years old,

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.360
compared to mostly
15 to 19 years old.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.240
Once you remove the study
with the age disparity,

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:13.360
the height disparity
also disappears.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.360
What about width disparity?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.840
Population studies indicate
that vegetarian diets

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.640
are associated with
a lower prevalence of obesity

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.680
in both adults and children.

